<block><txt break.before="1">An Act relating to the transfer of prisoners to
and from Australia.</txt></block></tier>
</content>


<content type="body">

<level type="part" id="pt.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_f29a52b5-e409-45e9-99f6-182bdaea4772"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="pt.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no><b>Part 1</b></no><heading guid="_cdab235c-d15a-4511-ad05-62d8ade007c9"
id="pt.1-he"><b>Preliminary</b></heading></head>

<level type="clause" id="sec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_aa20938a-c3f7-483e-a6ab-659965a9cd30"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>1</no><heading guid="_30b6e98a-c4cd-4470-9af7-92f12cc029c1"
id="sec.1-he"><b>Name of Act</b></heading></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">This Act is the <legref refid="act-1997-144"
jurisd="NSW" type="act" check="unknown"><name emphasis="yes"><i>International
Transfer of Prisoners (New South Wales) Act
1997</i></name></legref>.</txt></block></level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_e45e4f2f-dcd0-4984-8262-28970bcae99d"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>2</no><heading guid="_ab35fbd9-052f-4da0-9314-1c533d18cc83"
id="sec.2-he"><b>Commencement</b></heading></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">This Act commences on a day or days to be
appointed by proclamation.</txt></block></level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.3">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_34638d8a-5050-46a6-bc37-524294c4328a"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.3"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>3</no><heading guid="_b2c773a8-f5c5-45aa-bd23-a195e934ca77"
id="sec.3-he"><b>Object of Act</b></heading></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The object of this Act is to give effect to the
scheme for the international transfer of prisoners set out in the Commonwealth
Act by enabling such prisoners to be transferred to and from this
jurisdiction.</txt></block></level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.4">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_eb9a5cb5-1bb3-49f9-890f-266743db46c7"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.4"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>4</no><heading guid="_e6e0ee7c-5ad7-42d3-9605-48b7acd0547e"
id="sec.4-he"><b>Definitions</b></heading></head>

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.4-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_3581a181-91ca-4514-8095-0fa13158a561"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.4-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">In this Act&#8212;</txt>
<deflist>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_7b195e1b-356f-49f2-aa5f-60509e34d302"
id="sec.4-def.CommonwealthAct"><b><i>Commonwealth Act</i></b></defterm> means
the <legref jurisd="CTH" type="act" check="unknown"><name
emphasis="yes"><i>International Transfer of Prisoners Act
1997</i></name></legref> of the Commonwealth.</txt></block>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_651f154f-3059-42b0-a83c-6b99526bba6c"
id="sec.4-def.correspondinglaw"><b><i>corresponding law</i></b></defterm>
means a law of another State that provides for the international transfer of
prisoners.</txt></block>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_083fe49d-2359-4a32-b409-a19e00242d6a"
id="sec.4-def.function"><b><i>function</i></b></defterm> includes a power,
authority or duty.</txt></block>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_5a4f843e-10a6-4005-b14c-96fc7887e628"
id="sec.4-def.State"><b><i>State</i></b></defterm> includes a
Territory.</txt></block>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_59cc9b9a-b8bb-4a95-be85-a6e0691810d2"
id="sec.4-def.thisjurisdiction"><b><i>this jurisdiction</i></b></defterm>
means New South Wales.</txt></block>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_c0380ac8-7535-4995-9fb3-aafc9678ab29"
id="sec.4-def.WarCrimesTribunal"><b><i>War Crimes Tribunal</i></b></defterm>
means the Former Yugoslavia Tribunal or Rwanda Tribunal within the meaning of
the Commonwealth Act.</txt></block></deflist>
</block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.4-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_e6b80d70-c73f-431a-8f3e-ec921a39a87f"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.4-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">If an expression is defined in the Commonwealth
Act and is also used in this Act, the expression as used in this Act has,
unless the contrary intention appears, the same meaning as in that
Act.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.4-ssec.3">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_21cd1308-d3e7-4fc1-b16a-d3193d641df4"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.4-ssec.3"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(3)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">In this Act, a reference to the Commonwealth Act
includes a reference to&#8212;</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_18d90230-6201-42a4-a412-2d31befb3f7f" id="sec.4-ssec.3-para1.a">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">that Act as amended and in force for the time
being, and</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_67b495e7-f811-4652-bed0-abe31badfc59" id="sec.4-ssec.3-para1.b">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">an Act enacted in substitution for that
Act.</txt></block></li></list>
</block></tier>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.5">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_cae5d12d-a1ba-449d-bfa3-6a5c0ba67cda"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.5"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>5</no><heading guid="_ee0557e8-7cba-470d-8b1c-e64cb2fc8a88"
id="sec.5-he"><b>Notes</b></heading></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Notes in the text of this Act do not form part of
this Act.</txt></block></level>
</level>


<level type="part" id="pt.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_a0aca94a-ec3f-4501-b37e-33b118be85e9"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="pt.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no><b>Part 2</b></no><heading guid="_e082143f-71ea-4c43-b8ef-01495a4cae6c"
id="pt.2-he"><b>Conferral of functions</b></heading></head>

<level type="clause" id="sec.6">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_805466a5-3d0a-4dca-8267-09f78edc588c"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.6"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>6</no><heading guid="_8321702f-e0d7-460d-815f-07960384a06b"
id="sec.6-he"><b>Powers and functions of Minister</b></heading></head>

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.6-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_a2436ac3-2e0f-4816-8c2c-97ba3f21cba7"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.6-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">A Minister of this jurisdiction may exercise and
perform any function conferred or expressed to be conferred on the Minister by
or under the Commonwealth Act and may delegate to an authorised person any
such function.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.6-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_3229936d-7d48-4fe1-9fd0-33467589e867"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.6-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">In this section&#8212;</txt>
<deflist>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_45046d6f-050e-4a05-88ee-55988ad44bd0"
id="sec.6-def.authorisedperson"><b><i>authorised person</i></b></defterm>
means&#8212;</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_2a8adb8c-ec27-412b-a4f1-b6d9a29c9079" id="sec.6-ssec.2-para1.a">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">the head, or other member of staff, of a
government department administered by a Minister referred to in subsection
(1), or</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_3fcc2fc7-f599-4ceb-8c89-0f776dfd88b2" id="sec.6-ssec.2-para1.b">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">any person prescribed by the regulations or
belonging to a class of persons prescribed by the
regulations.</txt></block></li></list>
</block>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_cdf1d8fd-509c-40b0-9b38-cd862d8544e7"
id="sec.6-def.Minister"><b><i>Minister</i></b></defterm> includes any Minister
who under the law of this jurisdiction can act for and on behalf of the
Minister.</txt></block></deflist>
</block></tier>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.7">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_ce4e9a12-62fb-4e22-a2e1-2b6610c02d39"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.7"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>7</no><heading guid="_1b4c2b61-d0dd-4069-9bb5-0901ee8def90"
id="sec.7-he"><b>Powers and functions of prison officers, police officers and
others</b></heading></head>

<pre type="auto-inserted">

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.7-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_70e72283-e4aa-4c83-b67f-608905a7ad61"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.7-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">A prison officer, police officer and any other
official of this jurisdiction may exercise and perform any function conferred
or expressed to be conferred on the official&#8212;</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_f97db95e-3ae5-4c36-ac62-e7492c57799e" id="sec.7-ssec.1-para1.a">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">by or under the Commonwealth Act or a
corresponding law, or</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_e4e6a76c-a8d6-4fd5-ac22-f814a372207e" id="sec.7-ssec.1-para1.b">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">in accordance with any arrangements referred to
in section 8.</txt></block></li></list>
</block></tier>
</pre>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.7-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_c473e565-40cc-4d4e-8e49-0bdd7835a96a"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.7-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">It is lawful for a prison officer, police officer
or other official of this jurisdiction&#8212;</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_8cacebee-550e-4ace-976a-baddcf22deb9" id="sec.7-ssec.2-para1.a">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">to hold and deal with any prisoner in accordance
with the terms of a warrant issued under the Commonwealth Act in respect of
the prisoner, and</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_059c6bd5-0183-4178-a647-b43091994f3d" id="sec.7-ssec.2-para1.b">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">to take any action in respect of a prisoner
transferred, or to be transferred, to or from Australia in accordance with the
Commonwealth Act that the official is authorised to take by or under that
Act.</txt></block></li></list>
</block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.7-ssec.3">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_9458e7f9-d9ac-41fa-92f7-5c64ab7d27f4"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.7-ssec.3"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(3)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">In this section, a reference to a prison officer
is a reference to a correctional officer within the meaning of the <legref
refid="act-1999-093" jurisd="NSW" type="act" check="unknown"><name
emphasis="yes"><i>Crimes (Administration of Sentences) Act
1999</i></name></legref>.</txt></block></tier>

<note type="legtext" guid="_b14c1b39-c29e-46cb-8246-69fd149b50e4"
id="sec.7-note"><heading guid="_ce66213e-1194-4c2e-a20b-1bc300a5e442"
id="sec.7-note-he"><b>Note&#8212;</b></heading>
<block><txt break.before="1">A number of provisions of the Commonwealth Act
require State officials to exercise functions. For example, a warrant may be
issued under section 30 of the Commonwealth Act requiring a prison officer,
police officer or other person to escort a prisoner who is being transferred.
A police officer of this jurisdiction may arrest a person escaping from
custody under section 56 of the Commonwealth Act.</txt></block></note>


<content type="historynote"><txt break.before="1"><b>s 7:</b> Am 1999 No 94,
Sch 4.32 [1].</txt></content>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.8">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_62e7e338-ab95-4860-b2ec-63b4a4f55b70"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.8"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>8</no><heading guid="_b10cecf8-f1be-47e8-a2cb-b47b9e5c70c2"
id="sec.8-he"><b>Arrangements for administration of Act</b></heading></head>

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.8-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_2c7295bb-461b-4428-9115-b628de41c133"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.8-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The Governor may, in accordance with section 50
of the Commonwealth Act, make arrangements for the administration of that Act,
including arrangements relating to the exercise by officers of this
jurisdiction of functions under the Commonwealth Act.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.8-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_ccef6a08-874b-4cee-9e0f-78d40bb0b4ac"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.8-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">An arrangement may be varied or terminated in
accordance with the Commonwealth Act.</txt></block></tier>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.9">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_22060b12-c414-479b-b744-b607cb973da3"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.9"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>9</no><heading guid="_b1f75cce-6a9d-47a8-a032-f6b9ea4cfb57"
id="sec.9-he"><b>Annual report</b></heading></head>

<pre type="auto-inserted">

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.9-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_c8d57470-5b26-41cd-bfaf-e1f6ad472231"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.9-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The State Minister is to prepare an annual report
for presentation to each House of Parliament on each relevant decision made by
the State Minister during the year and of the reasons for that
decision.</txt></block></tier>
</pre>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.9-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_1ea538f7-5c0e-456f-b5dc-daad8a5200d2"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.9-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">It is sufficient compliance with this section if
the annual report is included in the annual reporting information for any
Department for which the Minister is responsible prepared under the <legref
refid="act-2018-055" jurisd="NSW" type="act" check="unknown"><name
emphasis="yes"><i>Government Sector Finance Act 2018</i></name></legref> and
the regulations under that Act.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.9-ssec.3">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_cb33d8bb-00dd-493c-ad7a-613730d0d97f"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.9-ssec.3"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(3)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">In this section&#8212;</txt>
<deflist>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_c7eef189-bc6f-4857-92e6-705f522de8c9"
id="sec.9-def.relevantdecision"><b><i>relevant decision</i></b></defterm>
means&#8212;</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_374ee344-83ae-441e-be97-d6e1f8d7a398" id="sec.9-ssec.3-para1.a">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">a consent, or refusal to consent, to the transfer
of a prisoner from Australia on the terms proposed by a transfer country under
section 20 (2) of the Commonwealth Act, or</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_212d5ada-a53f-4364-8fcd-d81376386c5d" id="sec.9-ssec.3-para1.b">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">a consent, or refusal to consent, to the transfer
of a prisoner to Australia under section 27 (4) of the Commonwealth Act,
or</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_36119953-8200-42bc-b1e6-28f5c57cac45" id="sec.9-ssec.3-para1.c">
<no>(c)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">a consent, or refusal to consent, to the transfer
of a Tribunal prisoner to Australia under section 36 (3) of the Commonwealth
Act.</txt></block></li></list>
</block></deflist>
</block></tier>

<note type="legtext" guid="_f20dbbab-b012-4033-8fbd-798cba7f1d3f"
id="sec.9-note"><heading guid="_e62d0aa3-8ffb-4e92-befe-9894e4071a4a"
id="sec.9-note-he"><b>Note&#8212;</b></heading>
<block><txt break.before="1">The State Minister is defined in the Commonwealth
Act as the Minister of the State administering the law of the State relating
to the transfer of prisoners.</txt></block></note>


<content type="historynote"><txt break.before="1"><b>s 9:</b> Am 2018 No 70,
Sch 4.57.</txt></content>
</level>
</level>


<level type="part" id="pt.3">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_f481ea2e-c904-46f1-baba-86269395dbef"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="pt.3"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no><b>Part 3</b></no><heading guid="_eeb8b6cf-3929-4d8a-b35e-59e24d3d551e"
id="pt.3-he"><b>Enforcement of sentences of imprisonment of transferred
prisoners</b></heading></head>

<level type="clause" id="sec.10">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_953f61d8-492b-4c51-8874-7286ceb42183"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.10"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>10</no><heading guid="_3920ceec-0fa1-4e75-82b2-e64679f7ad2a"
id="sec.10-he"><b>Prisoners transferred to Australia</b></heading></head>

<pre type="auto-inserted">

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.10-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_134f4aa3-d228-4925-9f5a-7a2c58d8be10"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.10-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Any relevant enforcement law applies to and in
respect of a prisoner who is transferred to Australia under the Commonwealth
Act to complete serving a sentence of imprisonment in this jurisdiction that
was imposed by a court or tribunal of a transfer country (or by a War Crimes
Tribunal) in the same way as the enforcement law applies to and in respect of
a federal prisoner serving a sentence of imprisonment in this jurisdiction
that is imposed under a law of the Commonwealth.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.10-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_4fdb28f0-49af-4c3e-bcf1-67c2a4853081"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.10-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Without limiting subsection (1), enforcement laws
relating to the following matters are applicable to a prisoner or Tribunal
prisoner who is transferred to Australia under the Commonwealth
Act&#8212;</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_30a68c7c-4334-4a97-9cf7-19e978a4d44d" id="sec.10-ssec.2-para1.a">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">conditions of imprisonment and treatment of
prisoners,</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_9ca6d627-74d1-4296-92b1-675d11789bbf" id="sec.10-ssec.2-para1.b">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">release on parole of
prisoners,</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_6257ad69-85c1-4a38-8e61-c155bc9292a8" id="sec.10-ssec.2-para1.c">
<no>(c)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">classification and separation of
prisoners,</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_3b96b3bc-f93d-4867-b868-58e65358dbc1" id="sec.10-ssec.2-para1.d">
<no>(d)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">removal of prisoners from one prison to
another,</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_fa3847bb-5d45-4171-91b8-1328606f485f" id="sec.10-ssec.2-para1.e">
<no>(e)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">removal of prisoners between prisons and
hospitals or other places or between one hospital or other place and
another,</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_12734ba6-e373-4ae8-ba78-27a67439fcb3" id="sec.10-ssec.2-para1.f">
<no>(f)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">treatment of mentally impaired
prisoners,</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_7aa51903-e230-4640-896f-7c8458e892f6" id="sec.10-ssec.2-para1.g">
<no>(g)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">eligibility for participation in prison programs,
including release under a pre-release permit scheme (however
called),</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_4079e7d2-d86f-4ea2-8625-e324457e505a" id="sec.10-ssec.2-para1.h">
<no>(h)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">temporary absence from prison (for example, to
work or seek work, to attend a funeral or visit a relative suffering a serious
illness or to attend a place of education or training),</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_7a04044e-bd3c-4ba5-9070-3fb91dee57d7" id="sec.10-ssec.2-para1.i">
<no>(i)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">transfer of prisoners between
States.</txt></block></li></list>
</block></tier>
</pre>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.10-ssec.3">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_7fe91d64-7f6d-403d-84fb-37ba993afd29"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.10-ssec.3"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(3)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Any direction given by the Attorney-General of
the Commonwealth under section 44 of the Commonwealth Act concerning
enforcement of such a sentence of imprisonment is to be given effect in this
jurisdiction.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.10-ssec.4">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_7e7797c7-5c9d-477e-8a8d-3cdcfdb10932"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.10-ssec.4"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(4)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Any direction given by the Attorney-General of
the Commonwealth under section 49 of the Commonwealth Act concerning a
prisoner referred to in subsection (1) who is pardoned or granted amnesty or
commutation of sentence of imprisonment as referred to in that section is to
be given effect in this jurisdiction.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.10-ssec.5">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_f5a9c19e-7956-41d8-a3b8-d46fd4ca3daf"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.10-ssec.5"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(5)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">In this section&#8212;</txt>
<deflist>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_9065f32e-e2a3-4f83-a88e-0f5345c27845"
id="sec.10-def.enforcementlaw"><b><i>enforcement law</i></b></defterm>
means&#8212;</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_35c140c9-5b5c-4261-a45a-c5d758d7270f" id="sec.10-ssec.5-para1.a">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">any law of this jurisdiction,
or</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_c6cb93af-02c0-4c6f-b561-3e144d9690f6" id="sec.10-ssec.5-para1.b">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">any law of the Commonwealth or another State,
or</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_8b289690-9724-4fe7-89e8-4d849f1e531e" id="sec.10-ssec.5-para1.c">
<no>(c)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">any practice or procedure lawfully
observed,</txt></block></li></list>

<txt break.before="1">concerning the detention of prisoners.</txt></block>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_7be286c1-d3b8-49c1-a049-69767d693196"
id="sec.10-def.prison"><b><i>prison</i></b></defterm>, in relation to a law of
this jurisdiction, means a correctional centre within the meaning of the
<legref refid="act-1999-093" jurisd="NSW" type="act" check="unknown"><name
emphasis="yes"><i>Crimes (Administration of Sentences) Act
1999</i></name></legref>.</txt></block>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_5ed186bf-37db-41d9-93be-a8499e425215"
id="sec.10-def.prisoner"><b><i>prisoner</i></b></defterm>, in relation to a
law of this jurisdiction, means an inmate within the meaning of the <legref
refid="act-1999-093" jurisd="NSW" type="act" check="unknown"><name
emphasis="yes"><i>Crimes (Administration of Sentences) Act
1999</i></name></legref>.</txt></block></deflist>
</block></tier>

<note type="legtext" guid="_765d3b8e-6a73-4843-8486-7ea3368eede3"
id="sec.10-note"><heading guid="_6587785d-1f0b-459c-8049-bfbd1adb600c"
id="sec.10-note-he"><b>Note&#8212;</b></heading>
<block><txt break.before="1">See Part 1B of the <legref jurisd="CTH"
type="act" check="unknown"><name emphasis="yes"><i>Crimes Act
1914</i></name></legref> of the Commonwealth in relation to the imprisonment
and release of prisoners. In particular, see sections 19A (Detention of person
in State or Territory prisons) and 19AA (Remissions and reductions of
sentences) and Division 5 (Conditional release on parole or
licence).</txt></block></note>


<content type="historynote"><txt break.before="1"><b>s 10:</b> Am 1999 No 94,
Sch 4.32 [2].</txt></content>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.11">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_62491208-c674-4c43-b179-bf91c40b3c70"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.11"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>11</no><heading guid="_6ca341e3-93c3-4694-a284-467d3b4d6472"
id="sec.11-he"><b>Prisoners transferred from Australia</b></heading></head>

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.11-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_cb3cb8de-8be2-4c06-84f8-5871a850693b"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.11-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Except as provided by subsection (2), the laws of
this jurisdiction relating to the enforcement of a sentence of imprisonment
imposed by a court of this jurisdiction on a person cease to apply to a
prisoner on whom such a sentence has been imposed who is transferred from
Australia under the Commonwealth Act to complete serving such a sentence of
imprisonment.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.11-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_77705514-2543-4391-9bf0-20355ceba668"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.11-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Nothing in this section limits the power of the
Crown or of a court or tribunal of this jurisdiction to pardon, grant amnesty
or commute such a sentence of imprisonment.</txt></block></tier>
</level>
</level>


<level type="part" id="pt.4">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_2572bf12-a385-4a25-97d6-1dd33e6ffb24"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="pt.4"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no><b>Part 4</b></no><heading guid="_b781b75c-1a57-4328-b7f6-23020b44d63b"
id="pt.4-he"><b>Miscellaneous</b></heading></head>

<level type="clause" id="sec.12">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_565e2ed0-a407-404a-a8be-49365369c306"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.12"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>12</no><heading guid="_33c9f267-afb9-416f-b78e-9c36d398a366"
id="sec.12-he"><b>Regulations</b></heading></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The Governor may make regulations, not
inconsistent with this Act, for or with respect to any matter that by this Act
is required or permitted to be prescribed or that is necessary or convenient
to be prescribed for carrying out or giving effect to this
Act.</txt></block></level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.13">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_70172982-f3af-4985-bf59-866609826b3d"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.13"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>13</no><heading guid="_e9281598-7131-4c78-a76b-72ec90f951b4"
id="sec.13-he"><b>Review of Act</b></heading></head>

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.13-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_44478037-f1f8-424e-8755-e53ac107efbd"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.13-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The Minister is to review this Act to determine
whether the policy objectives of the Act remain valid and whether the terms of
the Act remain appropriate for securing those
objectives.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.13-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_71f1b31e-5e5a-4c12-b041-b0d5086e8d58"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.13-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The review is to be undertaken as soon as
possible after the period of 12 months from the date of assent to this
Act.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.13-ssec.3">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_3a8c5840-df73-4f5c-b220-7f0a5b32acfd"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.13-ssec.3"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(3)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">A report on the outcome of the review is to be
tabled in each House of Parliament within 12 months after the end of the
period of 12 months referred to in subsection (2).</txt></block></tier>
</level>
</level>
</content>


